---
// The overview index idiom, device 5 of 8: one entry — its title, its
// description, and the meta line under them. See IndexHeader.astro for the
// family rationale.
//
// Both writing indexes render this row and they must go on rendering the same
// one. Title and description are props because they are the same two strings
// on both pages; the meta line's CONTENTS are a slot because they are not.
// /writing/ puts a date, an optional "updated" date and the tags there;
// /he/writing/ adds the original author's Latin name in a <bdi>, because for
// translation work the author is the strongest scanning signal in the list
// (specs/pages/translations-index.md §2.1). The <p> those children sit in —
// its flex row, its wrap, its 8px/16px gaps, its mono eyebrow — belongs to the
// device and stays here.
//
// ── the title's hover ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// entry-list.css wrote `text-decoration: none` on the anchor and
// `text-decoration: underline` on its hover. The second is a SHORTHAND, and
// its reset half is load-bearing: it also puts text-decoration-color back to
// currentcolor and text-decoration-thickness back to auto, over the base `a`
// rule's --border-strong at 1px. The `underline` utility is a longhand and
// sets the line alone, so `decoration-current` and `decoration-auto` are
// written out beside it — they are the shorthand's reset, not decoration.
// Dropping them costs a hairline of underline weight at 22px bold, which is
// exactly the class of change that ships unnoticed (verdict §4.4, failure 1).
//
// `[&:hover]:` and never `hover:`: Tailwind v4 wraps `hover:` in
// `@media (hover: hover)`, which would delete this affordance on every
// touch device.
//
// The resting `no-underline` and the hover branch are the same property, and
// the emitted order decides which wins. Checked in 4.3.3's own output rather
// than trusted: variants sort after the unvariated utilities, so the hover
// rule lands second. `underline-offset-[0.2em]` matches the base `a` rule's
// value and is written anyway, so the offset is the device's own statement
// rather than something it inherits and could lose.

interface Props {
  href: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
}

const { href, title, description } = Astro.props;
---

<li class="pbs-6 pbe-6 border-be border-be-border">
  <a
    class="inline-block text-size-lede font-bold text-text-strong no-underline [&:hover]:underline [&:hover]:decoration-current [&:hover]:decoration-auto [&:hover]:underline-offset-[0.2em]"
    href={href}
  >{title}</a>
  <p class="mbs-2 text-size-meta leading-tight text-muted max-inline-[64ch]">{description}</p>
  <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mbs-3 font-mono text-size-eyebrow text-muted">
    <slot />
  </p>
</li>
